->D. The exact kernel of pi is the cyclic subgroup <c>. Indeed, if beta(v)=0, choose an integer representative a_j for each coefficient of the finitely supported v. Its reduction is zero precisely when j+1 divides a_j. Thus a_j=(j+1)*k_j for an integer k_j, and the image of the jth summand in G is k_j*c. Summing over the finite support places v+N in <c>. Conversely pi(c)=0, so every integer multiple of c lies in the kernel. This is the concrete kernel calculation; it does not assume a quotient splitting.\")),\n         Paragraph(Text(\"Now let f:Q->G be additive. For each rational q and coordinate j, write q=(j+1)*(q/(j+1)). Additivity shows that the jth coordinate of pi(f(q)) is j+1 times an element of ZMod(j+1), hence zero. Thus f(q) lies in <c>. Apply this conclusion at q/2: f(q/2)=k*c for some integer k. Then f(q)=2*f(q/2)=k*(2*c)=0. This proves that every such f is zero, while each equation n*b=c separately has the explicit solution above.\")),\n-        Paragraph(Text(\"For the single period-one return atlas, take the carrier G with deck translations and time map T(x)=x+c. A signed chart is A(t,z)=z+t*c for integer t. Its seam law is A(t,z)=A(s,w) exactly when t=s+k and z+k*c=w for an integer k; its normalized phase is the unique element of Fin 1. Thus the primitive base period is one, while T itself has order two. In the multiplicative ReturnAtlas API the deck group is Multiplicative G, with holonomy corresponding to c. The translation R_n(x)=x+b_(n-1) satisfies R_n^n=T for every positive n and commutes with every deck translation. These roots even commute pairwise because G is abelian. A coherent rational system of translations would instead be an additive map a:Q->G with a(1)=c, which the theorem excludes. Every map commuting with all deck translations is itself a translation, as follows by evaluating it at zero. Thus the same obstruction excludes a deck-equivariant rational action whose time-one map is T. Pairwise commutation supplies no denominator compatibility. This is a standard reduced torsion group construction used as an explicit sharpness example; no literature priority or physical continuity assertion is intended.\"))\n+        Paragraph(Text(\"For the single period-one return atlas, take the carrier G with deck translations and time map T(x)=x+c. A signed chart is A(t,z)=z+t*c for integer t. Its seam law is A(t,z)=A(s,w) exactly when t=s+k and z+k*c=w for an integer k; its normalized phase is the unique element of Fin 1. Thus the primitive base period is one, while T itself has order two. In the multiplicative ReturnAtlas API the deck group is Multiplicative G, with holonomy corresponding to c. The translation R_n(x)=x+b_(n-1) satisfies R_n^n=T for every positive n and commutes with every deck translation. These roots even commute pairwise because G is abelian. A coherent rational system of translations would instead be an additive map a:Q->G with a(1)=c, which the theorem excludes. Every map commuting with all deck translations is itself a translation, as follows by evaluating it at zero. Thus the same obstruction excludes a deck-equivariant rational action whose time-one map is T. Pairwise commutation supplies no denominator compatibility. This is a standard reduced torsion group construction used as an explicit sharpness example; no literature priority or physical continuity assertion is intended.\")),\n+        Describe.Lean(DescribeId.Create(\"infinite-root-fiber\"),\n+            DeclarationHandle.Create(\"D5/S3/ConceptDynamics/Coding/PrimitiveLifts/IndependentRootCoherenceSeparation.infinite_root_fiber\"),\n+            H(\"Every nontrivial root fiber is infinite\"), StatementSource.FromAuthor(Disp(InfiniteFiberStatement)),\n+            AssessedProvenance.FromRepo(), Blocks(\n+                Paragraph(Text(\"In this exact quotient G and for every natural m>1, the subtype of all x with m*x=c is infinite. An explicit injection from Nat sends n to u_n=(n+1)*b_(m*(n+1)-1). The defining relation gives m*u_n=c. Under the same residual projection pi, its only possibly nonzero coordinate is i_n=m*(n+1)-1, with coefficient n+1 modulo m*(n+1). Since 0<n+1<m*(n+1), that coefficient is nonzero. The indices i_n are distinct, so evaluation at i_n distinguishes u_n from every u_k with k different from n. This proves infinitude at every nontrivial degree, rather than at just one degree. Degree one has the unique root c. No integer linear independence is asserted: all these roots satisfy the common equation m*u_n=c.\")),\n+                Paragraph(Text(\"Consequently, finite-root-fiber compactness cannot be applied to these full root-choice sets: its finiteness hypothesis fails at every degree m>1 in the original counterexample. Infinite fibers alone do not exclude coherent roots. Here the separate proved facts that every additive map Q->G is zero and c is nonzero supply the actual obstruction to rational coherence. This coordinate argument is a repository derivation for the displayed group; it makes no claim of literature novelty or a new general compactness theorem.\"))), DescribeRole.Theorem)\n         )));\n }"},{"sha":"7e370ed5e893709e05cdd442da515c6bbb8e2eeb","filename":"D5/S3/ConceptDynamics/Coding/PrimitiveLifts/IndependentRootCoherenceSeparation.lean","status":"modified","additions":35,"deletions":0,"changes":35,"blob_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/blob/2ad83ffab7deb22ef8c82288a992d3cac99c17a8/D5%2FS3%2FConceptDynamics%2FCoding%2FPrimitiveLifts%2FIndependentRootCoherenceSeparation.lean","raw_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/raw/2ad83ffab7deb22ef8c82288a992d3cac99c17a8/D5%2FS3%2FConceptDynamics%2FCoding%2FPrimitiveLifts%2FIndependentRootCoherenceSeparation.lean","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-omega-institute/trureturing/contents/D5%2FS3%2FConceptDynamics%2FCoding%2FPrimitiveLifts%2FIndependentRootCoherenceSeparation.lean?ref=2ad83ffab7deb22ef8c82288a992d3cac99c17a8","patch":"@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@\n \n import Mathlib.Algebra.DirectSum.Basic\n import Mathlib.Data.ZMod.Basic\n+import Mathlib.Data.Fintype.EquivFin\n import Mathlib.GroupTheory.QuotientGroup.Basic\n import Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp\n import Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith\n@@ -194,4 +195,38 @@ theorem independent_roots_without_rational_coherence :\n   obtain ⟨j, rfl⟩ := Nat.exists_eq_succ_of_ne_zero (Nat.ne_of_gt hn)\n   exact ⟨root j, root_relation j⟩\n \n+/-- Every nontrivial degree has infinitely many actual roots of the same element c. -/\n+theorem infinite_root_fiber (m : ℕ) (hm : 1 < m) : Infinite {x : G // m • x = c} := by\n+  let i : ℕ → ℕ := fun n => m * (n + 1) - 1\n+  have hi (n : ℕ) : i n + 1 = m * (n + 1) := by\n+    dsimp [i]\n+    exact Nat.sub_add_cancel (by nlinarith)\n+  have hi_inj : Function.Injective i := by\n+    intro n k h\n+    have hmul : m * (n + 1) = m * (k + 1) := by rw [← hi n, ← hi k, h]\n+    have hsucc : n + 1 = k + 1 := (mul_left_cancel₀ (by omega : m ≠ 0)) hmul\n+    omega\n+  have hproj (j : ℕ) :\n+      projection (root j) = DirectSum.of (fun t => ZMod (t + 1)) j 1 := by\n+    change beta (generator j) = _\n+    simp [beta, generator, reduction]\n+  let F : ℕ → {x : G // m • x = c} := fun n =>\n+    ⟨(n + 1) • root (i n), by\n+      rw [← mul_nsmul', ← hi n, root_relation]⟩\n+  apply Infinite.of_injective F\n+  intro n k h\n+  by_contra hnk\n+  have hik : i n ≠ i k := fun he => hnk (hi_inj he)\n+  have he := congrArg (fun x : {x : G // m • x = c} => projection x.val (i n)) h\n+  change projection ((n + 1) • root (i n)) (i n) =\n+    projection ((k + 1) • root (i k)) (i n) at he\n+  rw [map_nsmul, map_nsmul, hproj, hproj, DFinsupp.nsmul_apply,\n+    DFinsupp.nsmul_apply, DirectSum.of_eq_same,\n+    DirectSum.of_eq_of_ne _ _ _ hik] at he\n+  simp only [nsmul_eq_mul, mul_one, mul_zero] at he\n+  have hlt : n + 1 < i n + 1 := by rw [hi]; nlinarith\n+  have hv := congrArg ZMod.val he\n+  rw [ZMod.val_natCast_of_lt hlt, ZMod.val_zero] at hv\n+  omega\n+\n end D5.S3.ConceptDynamics.Coding.PrimitiveLifts.IndependentRootCoherenceSeparation"},{"sha":"31c3dc03d3840b7d79efb8ac4468b69848aa08b7","filename":"Golden/Frozen/state/D5/S3/ConceptDynamics/Coding/PrimitiveLifts/IndependentRootCoherenceSeparation.lean.json","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1,"changes":2,"blob_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/blob/2ad83ffab7deb22ef8c82288a992d3cac99c17a8/Golden%2FFrozen%2Fstate%2FD5%2FS3%2FConceptDynamics%2FCoding%2FPrimitiveLifts%2FIndependentRootCoherenceSeparation.lean.json","raw_url":"https://github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing/raw/2ad83ffab7deb22ef8c82288a992d3cac99c17a8/Golden%2FFrozen%2Fstate%2FD5%2FS3%2FConceptDynamics%2FCoding%2FPrimitiveLifts%2FIndependentRootCoherenceSeparation.lean.json","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/the-omega-institute/trureturing/contents/Golden%2FFrozen%2Fstate%2FD5%2FS3%2FConceptDynamics%2FCoding%2FPrimitiveLifts%2FIndependentRootCoherenceSeparation.lean.json?ref=2ad83ffab7deb22ef8c82288a992d3cac99c17a8","patch":"@@ -1 +1 @@\n-{\"statement_id\":\"sha256:a21955f56d62893fdf3ff2490a25a6fa5fec3265c816be6d5f669b46cd00284d\",\"declarations\":[{\"declaration_name_key\":\"ns(ns(ns(n0,4:ZMod),7:castHom),10:congr_simp)\",\"kind\":\"theorem\"},{\"declaration_name_key\":\"ns(ns(ns(ns(ns(ns(ns(n0,2:D5),2:S3),15:ConceptDynamics),6:Coding),14:PrimitiveLifts),34:IndependentRootCoherenceSeparation),10:projection)\",\"kind\":\"def\"},{\"declaration_name_key\":\"ns(ns(ns(ns(ns(ns(ns(n0,2:D5),2:S3),15:ConceptDynamics),6:Coding),14:PrimitiveLifts),34:IndependentRootCoherenceSeparation),1:B)\",\"kind\":\"def\"},{\"declaration_name_key\":\"ns(ns(ns(ns(ns(ns(ns(n0,2:D5),2:S3),15:ConceptDynamics),6:Coding),14:PrimitiveLifts),34:IndependentRootCoherenceSeparation),1:D)\",\"kind\":\"def\"},{\"declaration_name_key\":\"ns(ns(ns(ns(ns(ns(ns(n0,2:D5),2:S3),15:ConceptDynamics),6:Coding),14:PrimitiveLifts),34:IndependentRootCoherenceSeparation),1:G)\",\"kind\":\"def\"},{\"declaration_name_key\":\"ns(ns(ns